// Repository-local markdown lint settings, layered over the shared rule set.
//
// `content-build markdown` passes the shared rules (engine/prose-config.mjs) as
// markdownlint-cli2's `optionsDefault`, and this file is merged over them **key
// by key**. So the rule set survives — `default: false` and every rule enabled
// by name still apply — but `ignores` here *replaces* the shared
// `MARKDOWN_IGNORES` rather than adding to it.
//
// That is why `CHANGELOG.md` is restated below even though the shared default
// already lists it: dropping it here would un-ignore it. Verified rather than
// assumed — with only the second entry present, `npm run lint:markdown` reports
// ten findings in `CHANGELOG.md`.
{
    "ignores": [
        // Assembled by `changeset version` from the `.changeset/*.md` bodies on
        // every release. Its findings report on the generator and on changeset
        // bodies already consumed and deleted, and the next release rewrites the
        // file — so they are real and unfixable at the point they are reported.
        // This entry mirrors the shared default; the reasoning lives there too.
        "CHANGELOG.md",

        // The published changelog of `@heroiclands/content-build`, a deprecated
        // repository whose package was absorbed into this one at 3.0.0 (#32).
        //
        // Frozen, not merely generated: exactly one commit has ever touched it,
        // nothing regenerates it, and it ships only because `files` lists it.
        // Its findings — two MD001 heading skips and one bare URL — are facts
        // about what content-build published, not style this repository is still
        // choosing. Rewriting them would edit a historical record to satisfy a
        // rule about prose nobody will write again, and would leave a style-only
        // commit in the blame of a file whose value is being what was published.
        "CHANGELOG-content-build.md",
    ],
}
